00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:02,386
Cent #1264.

2
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:06,879
A penny struck in 1944 with no mint

3
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:09,650
mark, generally indicating the Philadelphia mint.

4
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:13,880
22 of the 10,000 Cents are dated 1944.

5
00:00:14,519 --> 00:00:16,547
None is dated 1943,

6
00:00:16,573 --> 00:00:18,379
the year pennies were struck in steel.

7
00:00:19,359 --> 00:00:20,640
Coins from significant years

8
00:00:20,719 --> 00:00:22,550
have acquired a special resonance.

9
00:00:23,626 --> 00:00:26,160
In July 1944, at Bretton Woods,

10
00:00:26,239 --> 00:00:28,160
44 nations tied their currencies

11
00:00:28,199 --> 00:00:30,650
to the US dollar, and the dollar to gold.

12
00:00:31,679 --> 00:00:33,963
In 1971 that tie was cut.

13
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:36,060
The dollar could no longer be exchanged

14
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,060
for gold, and US currency became

15
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:40,680
fiat: worth what it is trusted to be worth.

16
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:43,240
CENTS keeps that question open:

17
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:45,570
what a cent is worth, and who decides.

18
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:49,600
1944 also makes this a Wheat Cent,

19
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:53,280
one of 208: from 1909 to 1958,

20
00:00:53,359 --> 00:00:55,652
two ears of wheat framed the back of the penny.

21
00:00:56,799 --> 00:00:58,159
This Cent is the oldest Gold

22
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:00,405
Cent in the collection, by 12 years.

23
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:03,240
The Traits Atlas of the CENTS Trait Council

24
00:01:03,359 --> 00:01:05,719
describes gold patina as a luminous surface

25
00:01:05,799 --> 00:01:08,140
toning, suspended between metal and light.

26
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:10,375
This one is Notable Gold.

27
00:01:10,972 --> 00:01:13,480
The other grade, Full, is a continuous golden

28
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:14,680
sheen over more than about

29
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:16,308
70 percent of the surface.

30
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:19,439
69 Cents carry gold.

31
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:22,379
Every other one was struck in 1956 or later.

32
00:01:24,599 --> 00:01:27,280
Over Lincoln's head lies Significant Obsidian:

33
00:01:27,319 --> 00:01:29,799
in the Atlas's words, a major visual actor

34
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:32,620
with strong darkening, but not yet fully dominant.

35
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:35,099
The unique form of the obsidian on this

36
00:01:35,219 --> 00:01:37,995
Cent is what gives it its nickname: the Alien Cent.

37
00:01:39,019 --> 00:01:40,459
Near the rim, a fleck of paint

38
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:42,132
marks it as Contaminated.

39
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:45,400
Compare Cent #543,

40
00:01:45,439 --> 00:01:48,153
also from 1944, with no visual trait.

41
00:01:48,799 --> 00:01:50,379
Only one of them turned gold.

42
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:52,819
Struck in the year the dollar was

43
00:01:52,859 --> 00:01:54,819
tied to gold, and now toned the colour

44
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:57,353
